<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahathir Mohamad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1925">1925</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mahathir Mohamad is a Malaysian politician who was prime minister from 1981 to 2003 and again from 2018 to 2020. His first long tenure brought rapid industrialisation and large infrastructure projects, but also curbs on the judiciary and the rulers' powers and the jailing of his deputy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anwar-ibrahim">Anwar Ibrahim</a>. At 92 he returned to power at the head of the opposition alliance that defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barisan-nasional">Barisan Nasional</a> in 2018.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mahathir-mohamad.jpg" alt="Mahathir Mohamad" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: kremlin.ru · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahathir_Mohamad_13112018_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
